  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "as for layers, my process usually involves as few layers as possible! (cause i focused a Lot on traditional methods while shifting from an illustrative style to painterly) when im making big adjustments, or moving along the rendering pipeline in a noticeable way, ill often make a new layer to paint ontop of only so i can switch it on and off to check if the previous 'version' looked better for any particular reason. but as soon as im ready to move on i merge it with the layer below and repeat those steps. (that's why my progress photos are laid out Like That. i take screenshots at various points to show my wife cause without them im left with the final portrait on a single layer and like... the background color layer sdkfsjkd)"
  }
